{
  "$comment": "DDD bridge for PatternFly 6. Build with: yarn ddd:bridge elements/patternfly-theme. Named DDD colors are constants (elements pair them with light-dark() themselves), so they point at fixed PatternFly palette values by role; mode-aware PatternFly semantic tokens are used for the theme chrome and for fonts, radius, shadows and focus. Tiers follow elements/d-d-d/design-system/bridge/contract.json. Kept as DDD on purpose: font-weight light and medium (PatternFly has no 300 or 500 step), radius-xl and boxShadow-xl (no PatternFly equivalent), timing-emphasized, state opacities and control heights (PatternFly has no tokens for them), and the semantic type sizes: PatternFly body text is 14px (below the 16px floor) and its h3-h6 (18px, 16px) would fall below DDD's 20px body text, so headings follow DDD until body size is decided.",
  "system": "patternfly",
  "title": "PatternFly",
  "prefix": "Patternfly",
  "homepage": "https://www.patternfly.org",
  "sources": [
    {
      "package": "@patternfly/patternfly",
      "version": "6.7.0",
      "license": "MIT",
      "copyright": "Copyright (c) 2019 Red Hat, Inc.",
      "homepage": "https://www.patternfly.org",
      "repository": "https://github.com/patternfly/patternfly",
      "format": "css",
      "file": "base/patternfly-variables.css",
      "scopes": {
        "light": [":root"],
        "dark": [":root", ":root:where(.pf-v6-theme-dark)"]
      }
    }
  ],
